.TH UBUNTU-CN-INPUT-MEMORY 1 "2026-11-24" "Xiapin 2.0.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ubuntu-cn-input-memory \- manage Xiapin local learning data
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ubuntu-cn-input-memory
.BR status | migrate
.br
.B ubuntu-cn-input-memory
.BR export | backup
.RI [ output.ucimem ]
.br
.B ubuntu-cn-input-memory verify
.I archive.ucimem
.br
.B ubuntu-cn-input-memory
.BR import | restore
.I archive.ucimem
.RB [ --replace ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Xiapin stores its private LibIME user dictionary and history below
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/xiapin ,
or below
.I ~/.local/share/xiapin
when XDG_DATA_HOME is unset.
.PP
This command exports data to a versioned ZIP container, validates names, sizes,
UTF-8 and SHA-256 checksums, and imports data atomically. Archives use mode 0600.
They are integrity protected but are not encrypted.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Print active data paths and any legacy paths available for migration.
.TP
.B export, backup
Export learning data. With no path, create a timestamped state-directory archive.
.TP
.B verify
Validate an archive without changing user data.
.TP
.B import, restore
Merge an archive into current data. Use
.B --replace
to replace current data. A backup is made before writing.
.TP
.B migrate
Import learning data from a Xiapin 1.x Fcitx or older Table path when 2.0 private
files do not yet exist.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/xiapin/user.dict
Private LibIME user dictionary.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/xiapin/user.history
Private LibIME history.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/ubuntu-cn-input/memory/backups/
Default exports and pre-import backups.
.SH PRIVACY
Archives may contain names, project terms and entered phrases. Store and move
them using trusted or encrypted media. Xiapin does not upload them.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ibus (1)
